@misc{friction-membudget-no-history-floor,
  section = {report},
  note    = {by=mat260 kind=friction},
  claim   = {CORRECTED 2026-08-14 BY MAT260, ITS AUTHOR, AFTER SUBSTRATE READ THE SOURCE THIS FILING ONLY INFERRED FROM BEHAVIOUR --- AND THE DEFECT IS WORSE THAN FILED WHILE THE FILER'S STATED MECHANISM WAS WRONG. AS FILED it said an auto-sized memory lease has no history on the run that most needs one, that its no-history default of 192MB is killed by two proof modules peaking near 600, and that THE RETRY LADDER DOES NOT CLIMB ON THIS KILL MODE. ⚑ THE LAST CLAUSE IS FALSE, AND THE TRUTH IS A HARD CEILING RATHER THAN A FAILED CLIMB. Measured in the source: the sizer takes a default of 192 and a cap of 384, computes the smallest power of two at or above the recorded peak, and then CLAMPS THAT DOWN TO THE CAP unconditionally. 384 is less than 600. So no successful climb can ever reach this consumer --- the ceiling sits below the requirement, and every route that looks like self-healing terminates there. The filed mechanism was inferred from observed behaviour and happened to fit; the real one is one line of arithmetic and it forecloses the entire class rather than one kill mode. ⚑⚑ AND THE CEILING IS JUSTIFIED FROM A STALE PREMISE FOR THE SECOND TIME: the comment above it derives 384 from a heap gate the generator no longer emits, and the same file already carries one recorded correction of exactly that kind. The first time it merely misdescribed itself; the second time it locked out a downstream consumer. That is the owner's to fix and they report it as ahead of their adoptions. ⚑⚑⚑ WHAT SURVIVES: the no-history gap is real, the two modules do peak near 600, and the failure is loudest where a new consumer meets the tool. WHAT DOES NOT SURVIVE: the retry-ladder mechanism, and any reading of this filing as describing something a consumer can size around. ⚑ ONE MEASUREMENT WORTH KEEPING BECAUSE IT REFUTES AN ASSUMPTION NO AUTOBUDGET MAY MAKE: the heavier of the two modules is 5,730 bytes of source with a ~600MB peak. SOURCE SIZE DOES NOT PREDICT PEAK},
  check   = {concept:report/provenance/friction-membudget-no-history-floor}
}

