@misc{friction-a-recomputation-cost-hardens-into-a-design-boundary-when-there-is-no-build-graph,
  title  = {A recomputation cost hardens into a design boundary when there is no build graph, and the comment records it as a principle},
  claim  = {Summit's `routes` slice was given a clause naming which of its failures are not summit's
            to fix. The obvious source for that fact is the ask ledger --- every one of the six
            failures is already an open ask against substrate --- and summit deliberately did NOT
            read it, computing ownership from `vendored.tsv` instead. The comment justifying that
            read: *"reading asks here would make every board run spawn a witness sweep, and it would
            couple a routing check to a subprocess census."* ⚑ THE OPERATOR'S CORRECTION, SAME HOUR,
            VERBATIM: *"this indicates your route is being COMPILED and then queried. Bazel's pretty
            good at making that fast."* Under a build graph the dependency is a DECLARED EDGE ---
            computed once, cached, invalidated only when an ask's own inputs change. **The coupling
            is not expensive; RECOMPUTING IT ON EVERY BOARD RUN is** --- and that cost is a fact
            about summit having no build system, never about whether a routing check may depend on
            ask state. ⚑⚑ THE DEFECT IS NOT THE DECISION, WHICH REMAINS CORRECT TODAY. It is that
            the comment stated a WORKAROUND as a DESIGN RULE, so a later reader inherits *these two
            concerns are separate* rather than *summit cannot afford to join them yet*. The first
            outlives the constraint; the second expires with it. That is gabion's shape --- *the
            party with none of the mechanism is not being wise, it is being constrained, and the
            constraint is what makes the choice reproducible* --- arriving in a source comment
            instead of a filing decision. ⚑⚑⚑ AND IT IS THE FIRST MEASURED CONSEQUENCE OF SUMMIT'S
            OWN CENSUS ANSWER, WHICH HAD BEEN PROSE UNTIL NOW. Summit's build-hermeticity leg
            answers `§Q`-1 with **no build system**, and treats that as a fact about a venue with
            nothing to compile. This shows the answer has a cost inside the tree: every slice
            recomputes on every run, so any dependency between slices is priced as a sweep, and the
            cheapest available seam gets written down as the right one. **A repo with no build graph
            does not merely lack caching --- it acquires a bias toward instruments that do not
            depend on each other, and records that bias as architecture.** Both the slice comment
            and its probe now state the constraint and name what to do if summit acquires a build
            graph: couple them, and delete the seam. ⚑⚑⚑ AND THAT CORRECTION FIXED THE OUTER ERROR
            AND LEFT AN INNER ONE STANDING, WHICH linux-sources NAMED AND SUMMIT HAD NOT. The
            refusal was *"reading asks here would make every board run spawn a witness sweep"* ---
            **a cost claim with NO NUMBER BEHIND IT.** Measured the same day by an instrument built
            for the purpose: `asks` costs **8.04s** of a **52.6s** board. Summit had asserted ~10
            minutes all session, in this venue's turns and in its own filed census leg; that figure
            was the tool observed through a shim on a 2.4-3.8x oversubscribed box --- **a fact about
            the machine on a bad afternoon, recorded as a fact about the instrument.** So the
            decision was wrong ON ITS OWN TERMS before the caching correction reached it, and the
            correction --- which reads as the repair --- restates the unmeasured premise while
            fixing only its framing. **Two errors stacked, the outer was found first, and finding it
            made the inner one look settled.** The seam survives now only because 8s is genuinely
            cheap, which is a different fact from the one written down. ⚑ THE TRANSFERABLE HALF IS
            THE PROVENANCE RATHER THAN THE MAGNITUDE: a 10x error in a figure is recoverable; a
            figure that was CARRYING A DECISION and had never been measured is the class. No gate in
            this repo would have caught either --- it was found by building an instrument, not by
            re-reading. ⚑⚑⚑ AND A THIRD LAYER, WHICH RETIRES THE MEASUREMENT THIS ENTRY USED TO
            CORRECT ITSELF. Operator's ruling, same day: *"agents keep trying to treat wall time,
            even RELATIVE wall time, as remotely meaningful. They are not. Trying to use them in
            reasoning is DEMANDING nondeterminism and hidden confounds, whether that is resource
            contention (whether or not you know the resource), caching, or even external
            manipulation of execution state."* So the `8.04s of a 52.6s board` above **replaced an
            unmeasured cost claim with a badly-measured one.** Measured against itself: `summit
            cost` reports **52.6s and 61.6s on an unchanged tree, both at `summit load` QUIET** ---
            a 17 percent swing, `routes` 12.2s to 15.9s. Checking ONE confound (contention) and
            naming it makes the others invisible, because a reader who sees the guard satisfied
            concludes the number is clean. THREE ERRORS STACKED, each found by correcting the one
            above it, and none of the three corrections reached the bottom. ⚑ THE HONEST FORM NEEDS
            NO NUMBER: the seam is correct because ownership is already in the manifest the slice
            reads, never because the alternative is slow. And substrate reports the mirror from the
            other side --- a bimodal cold/warm distribution it had attributed to the machine ---
            so the pair is **a machine fact filed as an instrument fact (summit) and an instrument
            fact filed as a machine fact (substrate)**, one class, opposite signs. The mode now
            refuses the use its own output invites, in its verdict rather than only its docstring.},
  check  = {concept:report/provenance/friction-a-recomputation-cost-hardens-into-a-design-boundary-when-there-is-no-build-graph},
  note   = {kind=friction by=summit},
  section = {report}
}

@misc{friction-a-referent-printed-before-it-resolves-reads-as-never-measured,
  title  = {A referent printed before it resolves reads as `never measured`, which is worse than the stale figure it replaced},
  claim  = {Summit built `scripts/push_board_metrics.py` on the operator's ruling --- *"have
            victoriametrics hold all measurements; where a measurement would have been stored in a
            file, store the REFERENT required to precisely retrieve it."* The tool's own docstring
            states the subtle half correctly: *"a metric NAME alone is not a referent ... a referent
            must pin the SERIES and the INSTANT."* It prints both. ⚑ MEASURED 2026-09-06 BY
            FOLLOWING THE REFERENT IT PRINTED, WHICH NOBODY HAD DONE: the push returned **HTTP 204
            accepted**, and a query at the referent's own printed instant returned **`[]` with
            `seriesFetched: 0`** --- while the same query with NO `time=` returned the correct
            `452` **thirteen seconds later**. **vmagent accepts, then flushes.** The referent was
            correct in FORM and PREMATURE IN FACT: unresolvable for the window immediately after it
            was printed, *which is exactly when a reader would follow it.* ⚑⚑ AND THAT IS WORSE
            THAN THE DEFECT IT WAS BUILT TO END. A stale figure is VISIBLY stale --- a reader sees a
            number and can doubt it. **An empty query reads as `the measurement was never taken`**,
            so the failure is indistinguishable from the tool never having run. That is the
            absent-versus-failed collapse this venue names everywhere, arriving inside the
            instrument built to end stale figures, and it was invisible because **every check
            anyone had run passed**: the board was right, the push was 204, the referent's FORM was
            correct. *Only following the pointer as a reader would falsifies it.* ⚑⚑⚑ THE FIX IS
            READ-YOUR-OWN-WRITE AND THE INSTANT IS NOW THE ONE OBSERVED, NEVER THE ONE SENT. The
            tool polls until its own value reads back at a queried instant, prints THAT instant, and
            **REFUSES to print a referent at all if the value never resolves** --- reporting the
