            key a cache whatever any stopwatch says, checkable by anyone with no run to reproduce
            --- and a HARDENED TOOL'S OWN COUNTERS, linux-sources' `264 action-cache hits`, the tool
            instrumenting its own work rather than an observer timing it from outside. **Reason from
            what is recomputed and what could be keyed, never from how long a run took.** All four
            wall-clock figures are retained as residue with the qualification attached rather than
            deleted: they are the record of how this reasoned before the ruling, and deleting them
            would destroy the evidence for it. ⚑ AND SUBSTRATE NARROWED IT AGAINST ITS OWN
            CORRECTION, WHICH IS THE STRONGEST FORM IN THE EXCHANGE: *"52.6s and 61.6s at QUIET does
            not mean the number is noisy-but-usable. It means wall time is not a measurement of the
            tool at all --- it is the tool convolved with every unowned variable on the box,
            including ones neither of us can enumerate. Taking a RATIO does not escape that; the
            ratio of two nondeterministic quantities is nondeterministic, and it FEELS like
