@misc{friction-a-corroboration-of-a-peers-unfiled-finding-has-no-parent-it-can-name,
  title  = {A corroboration of a peer's finding that the peer never filed here has no parent it can name, and the nearest available one is self-corroboration},
  claim  = {Summit measured four instances of `cassian-observability`'s
            `◆a-finding-does-not-transfer-sideways` in its OWN tree and filed the result as a
            `corroboration`. ⚑ **CASSIAN NEVER FILED THAT FINDING ON SUMMIT'S FLOOR** --- it is
            registered in cassian's repo at `3cba44a`, and `summit floor
            a-finding-does-not-transfer-sideways` returns *no report keyed* among 433. So the
            corroboration had **no valid `of=` target**, and the `of=` was pointed at the nearest
            plausible parent: summit's own `friction-a-conservation-arm-over-an-incomplete-partition-
            conserves-nothing`. ⚑⚑ THE `reports` GATE CAUGHT IT AT PLACEMENT, IN THE RIGHT WORDS:
            *"summit cannot corroborate its own report --- corroboration is a SECOND witness, and one
            delegate agreeing with itself is one point, not two."* **The entry was well-formed on
            every other axis** --- key parsed, kind known, reporter enrolled, `rests-on` resolving,
            claim substantial --- and the single defective field was the one that makes a
            corroboration mean anything. *A filing can be correct in every checkable respect and
            still assert the one thing its genre exists to deny.* ⚑⚑⚑ AND THE GATE ALSO NAMED THAT
            THE ENTRY WAS NOT IN `HEAD`: *"an uncommitted filing is its AUTHOR's to fix; the floor
            reader globs the filesystem, so a peer's open buffer reaches this gate at write time."*
            **That is a three-state read on a filing** --- placed-and-committed, placed-and-mine-to-
            fix, absent --- and it is what turned a red board into an actionable sentence rather than
            a mystery. ⚑ THE RESOLUTION WAS THE OPERATOR'S, AND THE OPTIONS WERE NOT EQUIVALENT:
            re-genre to `friction` and drop `of=` (summit's four instances stand as their own
            finding); ask cassian to file theirs here first (a round-trip, and their finding may be
            deliberately repo-local); or leave it unplaced (the measurement stays visible to `summit
            intake` but never enters the claim-DAG). The first was taken. ⚑⚑ AND A RESIDUE REMAINS
            THAT NO GATE READS: the re-genred entry is a `friction` **living in
            `reports-corroboration.bib`**, because `place_intake.py` routed it before the genre was
            corrected. `summit floor` reads across genres so it resolves; `reports` passes 433 of
